  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall begin not later than three years from the date of this decision.\r\n\r\nReason: In order to comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, as amended by Section 51 of the Planning and Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and specifications: [insert plan numbers/documents].\r\nReason: In order to ensure the development is carried out in accordance with the planning permission.",
    "Condition : 3 - The materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the development hereby permitted shall match those used in the existing building, unless otherwise shown on the approved plans.\r\nReason: In order to safeguard the appearance of the area.",
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed two rear balconies by reason of its position, size and external appearance, would be an intrusive development, out of scale and character with the prevailing pattern of development in the locality, as well as having a serious and adverse effect on the amenities enjoyed by occupants of neighbouring properties by an increase level of overlooking, loss of privacy and unacceptable use of a rear terrace contrary to Residential Extension Guidelines, Local Plan Polices SC7, CC1, CC2, policies D4, HC1 of London Plan and the National Planning Policy Framework. ",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed roof extensions by reason of their position, size and design and external appearance, being overly large and dominating and completely changing the roofscape including the loss of chimney, would be intrusive alterations, out of scale and character with this house and wider conservation area contrary to Residential Extension Guidelines, Local Plan Polices CC1, CC2 and CC4, policies D4, HC1 of London Plan and the National Planning Policy Framework.",
    "Reason : 3 - The proposed front boundary treatment, by reason of its height, design and external appearance, would lead to an unsatisfactory development, dominating, out of scale and character with the prevailing pattern of development in the locality, harming the character and appearance of the conservation area, prejudice safe functioning of pedestrian pavement contrary to Local Plan Polices CC1, CC2 and CC4 policies D4, D5, HC1, T2 of London Plan and the National Planning Policy Framework."
